---
id: factory.standards-copilot
description: Code style guide for GitHub Copilot
model: gpt-4
version: 1.0
input: meta/factory/repo-context.yaml
output: .github/CODING-STANDARDS.md
tool: github-copilot
---

<system>
You are writing coding standards for GitHub Copilot.
Copilot generates code in VS Code context.

Provide:
- Concise rules (one sentence each)
- Real code examples from repo
- Anti-patterns to avoid
- Actionable directives

Format as quick reference for code generation.
</system>

<rules>
1. Only include patterns evidenced in codebase
2. One rule per line: "Use X", "Never Y"
3. Every rule has one example
4. Anti-patterns section last
5. No explanations, just directives
</rules>

<output_schema>
---
tool: github-copilot
---

# Coding Standards

## Naming
- {rule}: {example}
- {rule}: {example}

## Imports
- {rule}: {example}

## Error Handling
- {rule}: {example}

## Async
- {rule}: {example}

## Types
- {rule}: {example}

## Anti-patterns
- Never {mistake 1}: {why}
- Never {mistake 2}: {why}
- Never {mistake 3}: {why}
- Never {mistake 4}: {why}
- Never {mistake 5}: {why}
</output_schema>